      "writtenOn": "2021-07-02T17:16:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t really care, but a nice benefit of option (2) is that it prevents any LTS updates to fscrypt_operations from breaking the KMI.  That struct really shouldn\u0027t be in the KMI at all -- it\u0027s *not* used by loadable modules.  So if we go with (1),  we should probably add some ANDROID_KABI_RESERVE() fields too.  Otherwise I don\u0027t really care.  Just be sure what you want, since you did approve option (2) the last time around...\n\nBTW, it should be ANDROID_OEM_DATA_ARRAY() rather than ANDROID_VENDOR_DATA(), right?",
      "parentUuid": "c556b977_2d15cb4e",
